<p>Nepal votes on March 5 in an early parliamentary election, called two years ahead of schedule after youth-led “Gen Z” protests brought down the previous government. Voters will fill 275 seats in the House of Representatives, in a contest widely framed as a test of whether Nepal can steady its politics through the ballot box after months of upheaval. Coverage casts the race as a high-stakes faceoff between familiar party heavyweights and a rising, youth-driven political current. The field includes veteran leaders and prominent newer faces aiming to turn protest energy into electoral change. The election is also drawing close attention from regional powers, adding another layer of pressure on a small Himalayan democracy trying to regain political footing after the government’s fall. Still, some reporting points to a hopeful undercurrent: for young Nepalis weighing emigration for work, this vote has revived the sense that civic participation can still shape the country’s direction.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/o2GFCBV7ZJ347K2ATdtF_YjcXf68lHNA9vZ4EVqMZhFtRFmE4YAKtt1u8fxPf7-Uz9ggm9xllup19A0rv91VDYnK7YExsXV0pfHzB4kYvsD-TaWOsxQo7uFNH36XCrMADujZKBDai6E6DuxTEswTtT8gIJpIfI9zBPi_BxwjY7PlfBYnYICEECZEvYtmEkLU3xiLV4nv' alt='People attending a campaign rally in Kathmandu, Nepal, on Saturday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Youth migration: Christian Science Monitor says hundreds of thousands of young Nepalis leave each year for work. This election is giving some a reason to consider staying, because they see a real opening for political change at home.</li><li>Key contenders: The Guardian highlights a lineup that includes a Marxist former prime minister seeking a comeback, a rapper-turned-mayor appealing to younger voters, and a newly elected leader of the Nepali Congress party.</li><li>Election timing: Several reports stress that this is the first election since the youth-led protests. It comes nearly six months after unrest forced Nepal’s then-prime minister to resign, setting up an old-guard-versus-youth showdown.</li><li>Protest duration: The Hindu says the election was moved up after protests described as a two-day “Gen Z” uprising that threw the political calendar off course.</li><li>Voter scale: Firstpost says nearly 19 million eligible voters are expected to cast ballots in the high-stakes election.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Youth-led protest movement: Coverage describes Gen Z protesters pushing for political change—and trying to carry their demands from last year’s uprising into mainstream electoral politics. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/nepal-election-2026-gen-z-demands-political-change/article70702043.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Established political parties: Reports show veteran party leaders pitching experience and continuity, while newer figures argue the old guard failed to tackle corruption and basic governance problems. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/05/nepal-election-2026-voting-balen-shah-sharma-oli'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Election analysts: The Hindu points to regional “power plays” around Nepal as shaping the election environment, alongside the domestic goal of restoring constitutional order. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/nepal-goes-to-polls-amid-domestic-upheaval-and-regional-power-plays/article70703974.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/nepal-election-2026-kp-sharma-oli-gen-z-protests-key-candidates-parties-everything-to-know/article70706138.ece'>Nepal Elections 2026: Key parties and candidates</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/World/Asia-South-Central/2026/0304/nepal-elections-youth-migration'>Nepalis head to polls in first election since ‘Gen Z uprising’</a> - csmonitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/05/nepal-election-2026-voting-balen-shah-sharma-oli'>Nepal votes in election pitting entrenched old guard against a powerful youth movement</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/nepal-to-hold-first-parliamentary-election-since-gen-z-led-protests-toppled-govt-13986278.html'>Nepal holds first parliamentary election since Gen-Z-led protests toppled govt</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/04/world/asia/nepal-election-gen-z-what-to-know.html'>What to Know About Nepal&#x27;s Gen Z Election</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://apnews.com/article/nepal-shah-oli-protests-election-58cac72e25490c8c6363626a7dc10171'>Nepalis vote to elect 275 seats of the House of Representatives nearly six months after the Gen Z protests.</a> - apnews.com</li></ul>